# Which languages have the most native speakers?
subtitle: "Rank five great languages by native speakers, then see how the order flips when you count everyone who speaks them."
voices: {"a":"gemini:Orus | a firm, confident quiz host; plain and kind","take":"lines"}

## Which languages have the most native speakers?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Mandarin
      - Spanish
      - English
      - Hindi
      - French
    values:
      - [990, 484, 390, 345, 75]
      - [1184, 558, 1528, 609, 310]
    stage: 0
    sort: desc
    value_labels: true
    y_label: Millions
    icons:
      - {of: flag china, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag spain, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag united kingdom, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag india, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag france, set: twemoji}
sources:
    - id: eth
      title: 'Ethnologue: Languages of the World (2025 and 2026 editions)'
      authors: Eberhard, Simons & Fennig (SIL)
      year: 2025
      finding: 'first-language / total speakers, millions: Mandarin 990 / 1,184; Spanish 484 / 558; English 390 / 1,528; Hindi 345 / 609; French about 75 / 310'

    cards langs cites ["eth"] size 2 ends ["most","fewest"] hidden true
        * "Mandarin" icon.of "flag china" icon.set twemoji
        * "Spanish" icon.of "flag spain" icon.set twemoji
        * "English" icon.of "flag united kingdom" icon.set twemoji
        * "Hindi" icon.of "flag india" icon.set twemoji
        * "French" icon.of "flag france" icon.set twemoji
    text tag_nat "Native" #2f6b8f x 760 y 610 font_size 48 hidden true

    card title "Most native speakers?"

Five of the world's great languages. Which has the most native speakers, the people who learned it first, as children?
    draw langs

    ask "Put these languages in order of native speakers, from most to fewest. Drag the cards, then press Answer." on langs store r
        right: You got {r}.
        wrong: You got {r}.

    erase langs

Mandarin wins by a mile: nearly a billion people grew up speaking it.
    draw axes bar_1 tag_nat

Spanish comes second, with almost half a billion: carried across the Atlantic five centuries ago, it is now the home language of most of Latin America.
    draw bar_2

Then English and Hindi, close together at around three hundred and fifty million or so each.
    draw bar_3 bar_4

French, for all its fame, has only about seventy-five million native speakers.
    draw bar_5

    erase tag_nat

    text tag_all "All speakers" #b5482e x 760 y 610 font_size 48

But count everyone who speaks a language, natively or not, and the order changes.
    animate stage 1 duration 2.5

English jumps to first, with about one and a half billion speakers. Most of them learned it as a second language.
    highlight bar_3

So the world's most spoken language is mostly spoken with an accent.
    highlight bar_3 effect circle
---
